    <node id="&quot;数组&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An array is a data structure consisting of an ordered collection of elements, used in the context of the problem of defining a 'good array'."&lt;SEP&gt;"数组 (array) is the primary object being studied and manipulated in the task, with special properties like being a palindrome or a 'good array'."&lt;SEP&gt;"数组 is the central subject of the problem, being analyzed for the property of being a '好数组'."&lt;SEP&gt;"数组 is the data structure in this programming problem. It contains elements that can be modified by doubling a selected interval.数组 is the main object of manipulation in the problem."&lt;SEP&gt;"数组 is a data structure that holds a collection of elements, mentioned in relation to the permutation problem where each element has a specific range."&lt;SEP&gt;"数组 is a data structure in the student's program, which contains elements that can be manipulated."&lt;SEP&gt;"数组 is the collection of integers that 小苯 has"&lt;SEP&gt;"数组 (array) is an event-like concept in the text, referring to a mathematical structure that is to be transformed into a '双生数组' by 小红."&lt;SEP&gt;"数组 is the object being transformed into a '双生数组' through a series of operations."&lt;SEP&gt;The array that is being transformed to create a "双生数组", which is the central object of the problem and solution.</data>
