      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A palindromic array is defined as an array that reads the same forwards and backwards, providing the basis for defining what constitutes a 'good array'."&lt;SEP&gt;"回文数组 (palindrome array) is a type of array that reads the same forwards and backwards, serving as a key concept related to '好数组'."&lt;SEP&gt;"回文数组 is a property used in the definition of a '好数组', requiring specific symmetry."</data>
